it's known as a secure training center  this is oak hill in milton keynes but in  effect it's a children's prison  where young offenders from the age of 12  to 17 are kept and they can be there  after conviction or even on remand but  some of them  could be there  having been convicted of the most  serious crimes now of course like all  prisons they are from time to time  subject  to  inspections and in the case of a  children's prison it's by  ofsted the education watchdog the  prisons inspectorate and also the care  quality commission so there's a lot of  concern  over the way these places are run but  this is a very damning report uh in the  last few days  on oak hill um and what's happened today  is that  uh the re the inspectors have written to  dominic  raab the uh the new justice secretary  demanding urgent action  in effect it's asking him i mean in  theory he has 28 days to reply but in  practice in the in a very similar case  another center like this was shut down  within 24 hours and all the children  taken out and dispersed elsewhere so  that's a possibility that something like  that could happen but what we've got  here is a damning report on oak hill it  talks about  widespread failings very high  use of force by staff  frequent violence  among  those young children and in some cases  recently  um on average children were being locked  in their rooms for  19 hours a day but in some cases that  went up to 23 hours a day and as i said  we're talking about children as young as  12 here um  the letter to dominic raab highlights a  lot of these concerns um talks about a  dilapidated environment um violence and  use of force and often inexperienced  staff but it says this as well  systems for safeguarding children are in  disarray senior leaders failed to ensure  that safeguarding concerns and  allegations are referred to statutory  agencies as required there is a  considerable backlog of safeguarding  concerns awaiting action  children therefore remain at risk of  serious harm  so that letter calling for urgent action  just gone in to dominique raab and we  wait to see his response
 

